---
description: Security best practices for Python and JavaScript (tsp 前端 + 后端)
globs: *.js, *.jsx, *.tsx, *.ts, *.py
alwaysApply: false
---
# Security Best Practices

Ensures application security standards are maintained.

<rule>
name: security_practices
description: Enforce security best practices across the application
filters:
  - type: file_extension
    pattern: "\\.(py|ts|tsx|js|jsx)$"

actions:
  - type: enforce
    conditions:
      - pattern: "eval\\("
        message: "Avoid using eval() - security risk"

      - pattern: "innerHTML"
        message: "Use textContent or sanitize HTML content"

  - type: suggest
    message: |
      Security Best Practices:
      - Implement CSRF protection for state-changing endpoints
      - Use parameterized queries / SQL placeholders (never string-concatenate SQL)
      - Sanitize user input; never render unsanitized HTML
      - Implement proper access controls (authn/authz) on every endpoint
      - Follow security update protocol for dependencies (npm / uv)
      - Never commit secrets, API keys, or tokens; use .env + settings

metadata:
  priority: critical
  version: 1.0
</rule>
